          "distinct": false,
          "id": "f04f84328ec69f8bd982b44e655a594b05f37eb3",
          "message": "[service] Skip nodes without a built component in Graph.ShutdownAll (#16187)\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen a partial receiver reload fails to build a receiver, the fallback\nto a full reload is cut short by `panic: runtime error: invalid memory\naddress or nil pointer dereference`. On the first commit of this PR, `cd\nservice && go test -count=1 -race -run\n'^TestShutdownAllAfterUpdateReceiversBuildError$' ./internal/graph/`\nfails in `require.NotPanics`, and the stack shows\n`graph.(*receiverNode).Shutdown` called from\n`graph.(*Graph).ShutdownAll`.\n\nAfter the failed build, the receiver node is left with a nil embedded\ncomponent, but `ShutdownAll` in `service/internal/graph/graph.go` treats\nthe node itself as a component and calls its promoted `Shutdown` method.\n\nYou don't need a special test factory to hit this. Put a receiver that\ndoesn't support traces into a traces pipeline: config validation accepts\nthe reference, and the receiver factory only rejects the signal during\nthe build.\n\n`ShutdownAll` now uses `builtComponent` to skip nodes that have no built\ncomponent and keeps shutting down the rest. `StartAll` is unchanged.\nThis doesn't repair the graph after a failed partial reload, and it\ndoesn't have to: under RFC #14640 that graph is thrown away and rebuilt\nduring the fallback to a full reload.\n\n#### Link to tracking issue\n\nFixes #16261\n\nRelated to #5966\n\n#### Testing\n\nThere's one new test at the graph level and one at the collector level.\nFrom the repository root:\n\n```sh\n(cd service && go test -count=1 -race -run '^TestShutdownAllAfterUpdateReceiversBuildError$' ./internal/graph/)\n(cd otelcol && go test -count=1 -race -run '^TestCollectorPartialReceiverReloadFallsBackOnBuildFailure$' .)\n```\n\n`TestShutdownAllAfterUpdateReceiversBuildError` checks that shutdown\nskips the receiver that failed to build and still stops the other\nreceiver and the exporter. On the first commit of this PR it fails in\n`require.NotPanics`.\n\n`TestCollectorPartialReceiverReloadFallsBackOnBuildFailure` uses a\nreceiver factory that fails on its second build. Before the fix, the\ntest binary dies with a nil pointer panic and SIGSEGV in\n`Collector.Run`. After the fix, the collector gets back to\n`StateRunning` and the factory has been called three times: once at\nstartup, once for the failed partial rebuild and once for the successful\nfull rebuild. Both commands pass with `-race`.\n\nI left the existing start-failure test,\n`TestCollectorPartialReceiverReloadFallsBackOnFailure`, as it was, and\nno other existing tests changed.\n\n#### Documentation\n\nNone\n\n#### Authorship\n\n- [X] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
