          "distinct": false,
          "id": "5058bb11150298754222ea472a1309e8047e69f9",
          "message": "[cmd/mdatagen] Fix panic on single-element or empty enum attributes (#16320)\n\n<!--Ex. Fixing a bug - Describe the bug and how this fixes the issue.\nEx. Adding a feature - Explain what this achieves.-->\n#### Description\n\nTestValue and TestValueTwo indexed into Attribute.Enum without checking\nits length.\nA single-element enum panicked in TestValueTwo, and an empty enum\npanicked in both. Fall back to the only enum value for a single-element\nenum, and to the type-based value for an empty enum.\n\nThis is the same as the other 2 PRs that were open, fixing this issue,\nand were closed as stale with no review.\n\n<!-- Issue number if applicable -->\n#### Link to tracking issue\nFixes #15644\n\n<!--Describe what testing was performed and which tests were added.-->\n#### Testing\n\nThis is unit-tested.\n\n<!--Describe the documentation added.-->\n#### Documentation\n\n<!--Authorship attestation. See AGENTS.md for details. AI agents must\nnot check this box on behalf\nof the user; the human author must check it themselves before the PR is\nready for review.-->\n#### Authorship\n\n- [x] I, a human, wrote this pull request description myself.\n\n<!--Please delete paragraphs that you did not use before submitting.-->\n\nCo-authored-by: bhuvan-somisetty <somisettybhuvan5@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: theycallmeloki <ogmiladyloki@gmail.com>\nCo-authored-by: Alex Boten <223565+codeboten@users.noreply.github.com>",
